<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7635" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cētārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		cetus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to fish;</i> only <i>subst.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cētārĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m., <i>a
			fish-monger</i>, <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun. 2, 2, 26</span></i> (also in <i><span class="en">Cic. Off.
				1, 42, 150</span></i>); Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 49,
				15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 8, 17, 12</span></i>.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cētārĭus</span></b> , <i>title of a book of</i> C. Matius, <i><span class="en">Col. 12,
				46, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cētā-rĭum</span></b> ,
			ii, n., <i>a fish-pond</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hor.
				S. 2, 5, 44</span></i>.— Access. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cētārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, <i>f.; acc. plur.</i> cetarias,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				9, 15, 19, § 49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 5, 17, §
			66</span></i>; an uncertain form, <i>abl. plur.</i>
			cetariis, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 30, 48, § 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">31, 8, 43, §
			94</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
